WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.833
A bell rings. Right next to it, the
sound is loud. Far away, it is quiet.

2
00:00:10.053 --> 00:00:14.883
Where do sounds come from? What makes
them? And why do they get quieter?

3
00:00:15.383 --> 00:00:19.145
Tap a drum. Ring a bell.
A bird sings. Rain falls.

4
00:00:19.365 --> 00:00:24.798
Every sound comes from somewhere. The
thing that makes it is called the source.

5
00:00:25.018 --> 00:00:30.684
Boom. The drum is the source of that
sound. Tweet. The bird is the source.

6
00:00:30.904 --> 00:00:34.062
You hear with your ears. That
is your sense of hearing.

7
00:00:34.282 --> 00:00:38.879
Ears hear the sound. They do
not make it. The drum makes it.

8
00:00:39.379 --> 00:00:43.791
Pluck an elastic band. It
shakes so fast it looks blurry.

9
00:00:44.011 --> 00:00:49.398
And you hear a twang. A sound is
made when something shakes very fast.

10
00:00:49.618 --> 00:00:53.519
Scientists have a word for fast
shaking. They call it vibrating.

11
00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:58.105
Hum, and put your hand on your
throat. You can feel it shaking.

12
00:00:58.325 --> 00:01:02.272
Touch the band to stop it
shaking. No shaking, no sound.

13
00:01:02.772 --> 00:01:06.301
Stand right next to the bell
and ring it. It is loud.

14
00:01:06.521 --> 00:01:09.912
Take a step back and ring
it again. It is quieter.

15
00:01:10.132 --> 00:01:14.543
Keep going, all six steps. Every
step, the sound gets quieter.

16
00:01:14.763 --> 00:01:19.686
The bell is rung the same every time.
It does not make a quieter sound.

17
00:01:19.906 --> 00:01:25.014
The sound gets quieter on its way to
you. It spreads out as it travels.

18
00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:28.299
The further a sound travels,
the quieter it gets.

19
00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:33.490
Sounds can be loud, medium or
quiet. A drum next to you is loud.

20
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:37.286
A whisper is quiet. You have
to stand close to hear it.

21
00:01:37.506 --> 00:01:41.035
You can write it down in
a table, like a scientist.

22
00:01:41.255 --> 00:01:44.970
One step from the bell, it
was loud. Three steps, medium.

23
00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:49.788
Six steps, quiet. The further
away, the quieter it gets.

24
00:01:50.288 --> 00:01:54.003
Your ears hear sounds. Very
loud sounds can hurt them.

25
00:01:54.223 --> 00:01:58.774
Never shout into someone's ear.
Never bang a drum next to your head.

26
00:01:58.994 --> 00:02:03.081
Use sound makers carefully. Hit
a drum gently, with the stick.

27
00:02:03.301 --> 00:02:06.830
If a sound hurts, cover
your ears and move away.

28
00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:11.185
Every sound has a source. A sound
is made when something shakes.

29
00:02:11.405 --> 00:02:15.584
The further a sound travels from
its source, the quieter it gets.

30
00:02:15.804 --> 00:02:19.009
You can write loud, medium
and quiet in a table.

31
00:02:19.229 --> 00:02:21.969
And your ears hear it
all, so look after them.
